<title>NEW ZEALAND: INP unit lifts W&amp;H stake to 26.44 pct.</title>
<headline>INP unit lifts W&amp;H stake to 26.44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent Press Communications Ltd, a subsidiary of Independent Newspapers Plc said on Thursday it had raised its stake in New Zealand publisher Wilson and Horton to 26.44 percent from 23.69 percent.</p>
<p>IPCL is bidding for all of Wilson and Horton, offering NZ$11 or 1.375 exchangeable INP shares for each W&amp;H share.</p>
<p>Independent Newspapers and family trusts linked to principal Tony O'Reilly held 45.15 percent of W&amp;H prior to the bid.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
